# FreeBSD newsyslog.conf.d configuration for dpinger logs
# Place this file in /usr/local/etc/newsyslog.conf.d/dpinger.conf

# Dpinger monitoring logs - raw metrics data
# Option A: Size-based rotation (for variable load systems)
# These logs are high frequency (every second) and can grow quickly
# 30 × 10MB files = ~300MB total, ~143 days of data
# /var/log/dpinger_ix0.log        root:wheel    644  30    10000  *     NZ
# /var/log/dpinger_ix2.log        root:wheel    644  30    10000  *     NZ

# Option B: Time-based rotation (recommended for predictable retention)
# Daily rotation with 30 day retention = ~63MB total, exactly 30 days
/var/log/dpinger_ix0.log        root:wheel    644  30    *     @T00   NZ
/var/log/dpinger_ix2.log        root:wheel    644  30    *     @T00   NZ

# Network failover event log - human readable events
# Lower frequency but important for troubleshooting, keep longer
/var/log/network_failover.log   root:wheel    644  30    1000   *     NZ

# Configuration notes:
# - count 7: Keep 7 rotated files for dpinger (about 3-4 weeks of data)
# - count 30: Keep 30 rotated files for failover events (longer retention)
# - size 10000: Rotate at 10MB for high-frequency dpinger logs
# - size 1000: Rotate at 1MB for lower-frequency failover logs
# - flags N: Don't signal any process (dpinger handles this gracefully)
# - flags Z: Compress old logs with gzip to save space